 against cobit  19. kids between the ages of six months  and five years are the only age group in  canada currently without access to  vaccines but that could change shortly  based on promising test results by  pfizer ross lord reports  for the most part the very young have  been spared the devastating effects of  covert 19 but there are tragic  exceptions and in the united states  covet is blamed for hundreds of deaths  of children under the age of five an age  category that's not currently eligible  for vaccines that's likely to change  very soon based on clinical trials by  the pharmaceutical giant pfizer which  included three doses administered to  almost 1700 recipients over several  months  in a statement pfizer says our  formulation for the youngest children  which we carefully selected to be one  tenth of the dose strength for adults  was well tolerated and produced a strong  immune response  pfizer and his partner bioentec planned  to take their findings to u.s regulators  this week claiming the new vaccine is 80  percent effective the risks are minute  the benefits might be small given the  fact that the pandemic is waning to some  extent and the and the threat posted  children is somewhat small compared to  adults  but the comparing the two vaccine  absolutely outweighs the risk  epidemiologist ray watt deonandum  believes the vaccine will also remove  the fear factor for parents of very  young children  parents  like him for my kid for example is going  to day care in september i'm pretty  confident now that he'll have  some strong immunity when he goes to  daycare in the fall that's that's  exciting if approved by government  regulators the vaccine will fill a big  gap out of 85 million doses administered  in canada vaccination coverage is  highest in adults aged 60 and older at  almost 94 percent fully vaccinated  canadians between 12 and 60 are also  well protected in the mid to high 80s  there's a big drop to 42 percent for  younger children the under five category  is virtually empty with no approved  vaccine more than two years after the  pandemic started  regulatory approval could come within  days adding to pfizer's nearly  billion u.s dollars in covet vaccine  sales and adding another layer of safety  as the pandemic drags on  ross lord global news  the world health organization says it  expects to find more monkey pox cases as  it expands surveillance in countries  where the disease isn't typically found  but experts stress the cases identified  so far have not been severe  and the thing i just want to say here is  that this is a containable situation  particularly in the countries like where  we are seeing these outbreaks that are  happening across europe  in  north america as well  there are now more than 100 suspected  and confirmed cases in more than a dozen  countries including canada it's believed  the unprecedented spread may have begun  at two raves in spain and belgium  celebrating a man who was so much more  than a tap dance legend next  honey the 1969 fender mustang electric  guitar nirvana frontman kirk cobain  played in this 1991 music video has just  been auctioned off billionaire jim irsay  who owns the indianapolis colts bought  the guitar for a staggering four and a  half million dollars it was expected to  fetch only six hundred thousand cobain's  family is donating part of the proceeds  to mental health initiatives  ahead of national tap dance day on  wednesday some talented young dancers in  calgary are stepping up to salute a  legend on may 25th  tap dance great bilbo jangles robinson  was born as gil tucker shows us the  students are celebrating robinson's  legacy of promoting civil rights and the  dance style they love  tapping into something they can't get  enough of it's like a musical instrument  but like with your feet  so it's like a whole different like way  of making sound and making rhythms which  that's why i really like it excited  while getting ready for a big show this  